 Run tests with `npm test` (Node.js 22.18 or newer, with native TypeScript support).
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)` applies JSON Merge Patch as defined by
+[RFC 7386](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7386.html), returning an independent
+JSON value without mutating either input. Object patches merge members recursively;
+a member whose patch value is `null` is removed, and removing a missing member is
+a no-op. Arrays and all other non-object patches replace the entire target,
+including a root `null` patch. An object patch treats a non-object target as `{}`.
+An `undefined` target represents an absent document. Other inputs must be JSON
+values, with the same validation rules as `applyPatch`.
+
+```ts
+applyMergePatch({ name: 'Ada', settings: { theme: 'dark', old: true } }, {
+  settings: { theme: 'light', old: null },
+}); // { name: 'Ada', settings: { theme: 'light' } }
+```
